-- The macros: every op the cards use that is not a primitive, written over
-- the ones that are.
--
-- `docs/arena-ruleset-spec.md` §2 is the decision — nineteen primitives, and
-- one `DEFINE OP` here for each of the thirty-one rows `OP_CLASS` marks
-- *macro*. A macro is not a deletion: `power(…)` keeps its `OP_SCHEMA` row,
-- keeps printing as itself and keeps round-tripping by that name; this file
-- says only what it *means*, and `rulesets/expand.ts` is what lowers a program
-- written in these ops to a program written in the primitives.
--
-- **Most rows are not declared yet, and the table below is why.** Writing one
-- that silently dropped an argument would be worse than none: it would
-- validate, it would expand, the sweep in `scripts/verify/language.ts` would
-- pass, and the rule it claimed to explain would be wrong. Each row names the
-- one thing it waits on. The expander is built and tested against fixtures, so
-- the first row that becomes writable is a declaration here and nothing else.
--
-- ── what each row waits on ────────────────────────────────────────────────
--
--   param     answered (#273): inside a DEFINE OP body `$name` may stand in
--             every field position — a duration, a side, an area, a mode or
--             any closed list (declared `word`), a list of strings
--             (`strings`), a whole program (`ops`) — and in a selector's
--             count, `TOP n`, side and area. A row still listing it below is
--             waiting on the rest of its line, not on the grammar.
--   decline   `may` offers a program and the answer to take none of it: two
--             options, the second empty (spec §2.3). `chooseMode` drops an
--             empty option without asking, asks the master rather than the
--             `chooser` the call names, and binds no answer for
--             `did(what: may)` to read — the requirement §2.3 puts on the
--             primitive. Lowered today, "you may" would never be asked.
--   cause     `move` must carry a cause — `damage`, `ko`, `combo`, `effect`
--             and a plain draw are one move told apart by it, and the triggers
--             read it (spec §2.5-2). `moveTo` has no such field today.
--   subject   `modifyAttr` reaches one card and six attributes; the rows below
--             need a *player* and the *battle in progress* as subjects, and
--             `mode`, `markers`, `keywords`, `hidden`, `faceUp` and `flipped`
--             as attributes (spec §2.5-1, §2.5-3).
--   negate    the `negate` primitive — the general form of `negateSkills` —
--             is not an op yet (spec §2.2).
--   replace   the `replace` primitive is not an op yet (spec §2.2, #125).
--   cost      the `costModifier` primitive is not an op yet: a price is not a
--             number, which is the whole of spec §2.5-4.
--   audience  `reveal` shows a card to both players; `look` is the same act
--             with a narrower audience (20-11), and the field that says which
--             does not exist.
--   maths     an amount cannot subtract, so "until you have n life" cannot be
--             written (spec §2.5-5).
--
-- ── the thirty-one macros ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
--
--   op                   lowers to                waits on
--   draw                 move                     param, cause
--   discard              choose + move            param, cause
--   damage               move                     param, cause
--   mill                 move                     param, cause
--   addLife              move                     param, cause
--   lifeDownTo           move                     param, cause, maths
--   energyMarker         modifyAttr               param, subject
--   look                 reveal                   param, audience
--   ko                   move                     cause
--   switchMode           modifyAttr               param, subject
--   power                modifyAttr               declared (#273)
--   comboPower           modifyAttr               declared (#273)
--   grant                modifyAttr               param, subject
--   negateSkills         negate                   param, negate
--   negateSkillsOfKind   negate                   param, negate
--   hidden               modifyAttr               param, subject
--   redirectAttack       modifyAttr               subject
--   comboFrom            move + negate            param, cause, negate
--   flip                 modifyAttr               subject
--   faceUp               modifyAttr               param, subject
--   addMarker            modifyAttr               param, subject
--   removeMarker         modifyAttr               param, subject
--   costReduction        costModifier             param, cost
--   negateKeyword        negate                   param, negate
--   gains                modifyAttr               param, subject
--   replaceLeave         replace                  param, replace
--   altCost              costModifier             param, cost
--   resolvingPlay        replace                  param, replace
--   negateAttack         replace                  replace
--   negateCounter        replace                  replace
--   negateOwnSkill       negate                   param, negate
--   may                  chooseMode               decline
--
-- Three rows wait on nothing but a primitive that is only a field away
-- (`ko`, `redirectAttack`, `flip`) and three on `replace` alone
-- (`negateAttack`, `negateCounter`, and `resolvingPlay` once `param` is
-- answered). Those are the first this file should gain.

-- ── the two numbers a card changes (§2.3, 20-5) ────────────────────────────
--
-- A change to power or combo power is one act — one attribute of one card,
-- by an expression, for a duration — and `modifyAttr` is that act. The two
-- rows differ in nothing but which attribute they name, which is the whole of
-- the argument the spec's table makes.

-- §20-5 — "+5000 power for the turn", "+X power", "power +5000 for each …"
DEFINE OP power
  TAKES (target: ref, amount: amount, until: duration)
  DO {
    modifyAttr(target: $target, attr: power, amount: $amount, until: $until)
  }
  text: "the card's power changes by the amount, for the duration"
  doc: "what `power` means: one attribute of one card, changed by an expression until a moment"

-- §20-5 — "+10000 combo power for the turn"
DEFINE OP comboPower
  TAKES (target: ref, amount: amount, until: duration)
  DO {
    modifyAttr(target: $target, attr: comboPower, amount: $amount, until: $until)
  }
  text: "the card's combo power changes by the amount, for the duration"
  doc: "the same act as `power`, on the other printed number"
